{
  "id": 73107548,
  "iid": 478,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "ICMP: Fix dissection of Interface Information Object",
  "description": "If an address subobject was included, all subsequent subobjects (eg, interface name or MTU subobjects) would read from the same offset.\n\nFor the following packet capture, the current implementation of the ICMP dissector reads `10` (or `0x0a`) for both the beginning of the interface name subobject (eg, its length), **and** the beginning of the address subobject. The new implementation correctly reads the beginning of the address to be `0x0a` and the beginning of the interface name to be `0x3f`.\n\n[icmp-rfc5837.pcap](/uploads/3c2f9c1671c8195b336bc18bf554257c/icmp-rfc5837.pcap)",
  "state": "merged",
  "created_at": "2020-10-03T16:50:11.553Z",
